# Python bytecode from the repo's gate scripts (scripts/*.py) — never tracked
__pycache__/
*.pyc

# BMAD Method tooling is now TRACKED (reversed 2026-08-27, was untracked in
# 59c8d19 as "a vendored toolchain, not this project's work product").
#
# Why the reversal: the planning artifacts under _bmad-output/ are tracked and
# are the project's real sprint record, but the workflows that produce and
# maintain them were not — so a fresh clone (CI, a remote agent session, a new
# machine) had the outputs and none of the tooling. Recovering skills by
# reading them out of git history at 59c8d19^ works but is fragile and silently
# pins you to the pre-untracking version. Tracking the install makes every
# clone a first-class BMAD citizen and makes the method version an auditable
# part of the repo. Installed v6.11.0; see _bmad/_config/manifest.yaml.
#
# Personal overrides need no rule here: the installer ships its own
# _bmad/custom/.gitignore ("*.user.toml"), so _bmad/custom/config.user.toml
# stays local on its own.

# Retrospective/build review inputs — working artifacts, never committed
_bmad-output/implementation-artifacts/story-*-review-diff.patch
_bmad-output/implementation-artifacts/epic-*-review-diff.patch
cov/
.video_agent/

